{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Breakdown of all 7,007 bad-signature verdicts on the rewritten history, run with the veery build 91953e1ecf6 on 2026-11-18 PST. Each verdict was grouped by its SSHSIG key and by the env_id on its original raw event.\n\n- Live: 1,236 = 6e2a8414bf53 850 + 61689bf468f5 386. All have author 594c and writer env eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f. All are class A.\n- Ledger: 5,771 verdicts cover 5,528 unique (ticket, event) entries; the other 243 are the same entry counted again. Every one has `signer_pubkey: null`.\n  - Class A: 4,622 (6e2a8414bf53 2,377 + 61689bf468f5 2,245), all with writer env eea68b7f.\n  - Class B: 906, signed by keyring keys 3d4e271c8a89 (900) and a060aace07c3 (6). Their writer envs are b8a354e0 802, b2b5c498 73, ad49f17f 25, reconciler 4, and 2 others.\n- No bad-signature verdict falls outside classes A and B, so there is nothing new to file. The \"~700 remaining\" in the description came from the incorrect all-ledger split plus duplicate entries.\n\nFiled misogynous-archetypic-nematode for the operator: the rotated-out key 61689bf468f5 is still unrevoked. Not applied.\n\n**Blocker on implementing option (1): the trust config cannot express \"the environment the event was written from\".** Every class-A event carries `env_id` eea68b7f-…, which is the MCP tracker clone's `.env-id`. The keys are pinned under op-cert env 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65 (`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID`). Nothing in `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` or in the events links the two ids, and ledger entries carry no env_id at all; it is only on the retired raw file. An environment-bound check therefore needs one of these, which is a signing-policy choice:\n(a) Accept any pinned environment key, era-scoped, as a signer for any identity, with no writer binding. This needs no config change. It means anyone holding a pinned op-cert key can author as any identity.\n(b) Add a per-environment list of writer `.env-id`s to `trusted_environments.yaml` (for 9f1c8e42: eea68b7f). This binds the key to the box's writes. It adds a field to the trust config (Gerrit-gated, CODEOWNERS-protected), and ledger entries would read env_id from their retired raw file.\nClass B (the checker misclassifying 906 null-signer entries that verify) does not depend on this choice. Holding implementation until the binding is chosen."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795051512086980903,"uuid":"1c7859b9-3759-4241-935e-59a4e8ffd2df"}